# ROM images are copyrighted - never commit one, and the way back out of one
# that slipped in is a history rewrite.
#
# *.rom and hp48*.bin alone matched NONE of the names these files actually have.
# x48, Droid48 and Emu48 all use extensionless names, and decision 2026aug28
# says Agape48 bundles two of them - so the first `git add -A` after the assets
# landed would have committed both ROMs. Found by Windows-Claude on 2026aug31
# with `git check-ignore -v`, which is also the way to check any change here:
# reading the patterns is how this went unnoticed for a week.
*.rom
*.ROM
hp48*.bin
rom
roms
rom-*
gxrom*
sxrom*

# HP 48 state images. Same extensionless names, and "hp48" is the state file the
# core writes, not a ROM. Nobody should commit a calculator's memory either, and
# the state folder is easy to point somewhere inside a checkout while testing.
hp48
hp48s
ram
port1
port2
in-use

# src/core/x48/ is a vendored copy, not a submodule - it belongs in the repo.
